An example of a Stan model for analyzing time-series data is an autoregressive (AR) model. The Stan code might look like this:

```stan
data {
  int<lower=1> T; // number of time points
  vector[T] y; // time-series data
}
parameters {
  real alpha; // intercept
  real phi; // autoregressive coefficient
  real<lower=0> sigma; // standard deviation of the errors
}
model {
  for (t in 2:T)
    y[t] ~ normal(alpha + phi * y[t-1], sigma);
}
