To reference JavaDoc documentation in a LaTeX document, you can use the standard citation and referencing mechanisms provided by LaTeX. Here's a step-by-step guide on how to do this:

1. **Citation Management**: Decide on a citation management package. The most common ones are `biblatex` and `natbib`. For this example, we'll use `biblatex`.

2. **Bibliography File**: Create a `.bib` file to manage your references. This is where you'll add the details of the JavaDoc documentation you want to reference. For example, create a file named `references.bib` and add an entry for the JavaDoc like this:

```bibtex
@misc{JavaDocExample,
  title = {Java Platform, Standard Edition JavaDoc},
  howpublished = {\url{https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/}},
  note = {Accessed: 2023-04-01}
}
```

3. **LaTeX Document**: In your LaTeX document, include the `biblatex` package and link to your `.bib` file. Here's an example of how to set this up:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}
\usepackage[english]{babel}
\usepackage{csquotes}
\usepackage[backend=biber, style=authoryear, citestyle=authoryear]{biblatex}

% Link to your bibliography file
\addbibresource{references.bib}

\begin{document}

\section{Introduction}
As described in the Java documentation \cite{JavaDocExample}, ...

\printbibliography

\end{document}
```

4. **Compiling**: To compile your LaTeX document with references, you'll need to run a sequence of commands. If you're using `biblatex` with the `biber` backend, the sequence will typically be:

```sh
pdflatex yourdocument.tex
biber yourdocument
pdflatex yourdocument.tex
pdflatex yourdocument.tex
```

This sequence compiles your LaTeX document, processes the bibliography, and then finalizes the document with all references in place.

5. **Hyperlinks**: If you want the URL in the bibliography to be clickable, you can add the `hyperref` package to your LaTeX preamble:

```latex
\usepackage{hyperref}
```

By following these steps, you'll be able to reference JavaDoc documentation in your LaTeX document. The citation will appear in the text, and the full reference will be listed in the bibliography section at the end of your document.

