In Mathematica, you can use the `ScalingFunctions` option to apply custom scaling to the axes of a plot. This can be combined with piecewise functions to create a plot where the y-axis zooms in on a specific interval. However, as of my knowledge cutoff in 2023, `ScalingFunctions` does not natively support piecewise scaling directly. Instead, you can define a custom scaling function that behaves differently in different intervals of the y-axis.

