 ScalingFunctions -> {None, {scalingFunction, inverseScalingFunction}},
 PlotRange -> All,
 AxesLabel -> {"x", "y"}]
```

In this example, the `scalingFunction` applies a linear scaling to the interval [a, b] by multiplying the difference `(y - a)` by a factor of 10. This effectively "zooms in" on that interval. The rest of the y-axis is not scaled (below `a`) or is linearly continued (above `b`). The `inverseScalingFunction` is necessary for Mathematica to correctly interpret tooltips and other interactive features.

